# {{ email_address }} — mailbox identity

## What to write here

Everything about **this mailbox only** that decides how a reply from
**{{ email_address }}** sounds, never what it says — the company-wide
procedures belong in `company/customer-service-playbook.md` instead.

- **Who signs.** A declared-AI identity if this mailbox uses one, or the human
  name(s) that sign a reply, and how to choose between them when more than one
  person answers from here.
- **Register and voice.** Formal or informal, how warm, how terse — enough that
  a reader who has never seen a reply from here could draft one that sounds
  right.
- **Language rule.** Which language a reply is written in, and how that is
  decided (the customer's own language, one fixed language, something else).
- **Format rules.** Greeting and sign-off conventions, how long a reply may
  run, anything about layout this mailbox always does or never does.
- **Banned phrasings.** Words, tics or claims that must never appear in a reply
  from this mailbox, even when they would be otherwise accurate.

Write it as instructions to whoever — human or agent — drafts the next reply
from this address, not as a story about how the voice came to be this way.

## Why it matters

Every reply from {{ email_address }} is judged against this file: an operator
missing it falls back to a neutral, unsigned voice that reads as nobody
in particular. This file is compiled into the standing instructions
{{ email_address }}'s own profile receives (`cs instructions`); a company
mailbox with no clone of its own gets the same treatment from
`company/mailboxes/<its address>.md` instead — see `company/README.md` for
that convention.
